fix(nn): the arm set needed FOUR cells -- the depthwise pre-gate is a SiLU

Two adversarial reviews of the previous two commits. The first finding
invalidates the experiment as designed; the rest are guards that could not fire.

THE DEPTHWISE PRE-GATE IS NOT A GATE, IT IS A SiLU WITH A LEARNABLE SLOPE.
Since silu(y) = y*sigmoid(y), substituting y = a*u gives

    2 * sigmoid(a*u) * u  ==  (2/a) * silu(a*u)     for every a != 0

verified to 8.9e-16 in float64. The amplitude 2/a is constant per channel, so by
this module's own absorption argument it folds into that channel's depthwise
taps. What the pre-gate buys is ONE number per channel: the slope of a SiLU,
moved from after the convolution to before it, initialized at a=0 where it is
the identity. Only the POST gate is a genuinely new term, because it reads
position t while the conv output mixes t-j.

So "gated_conv=True, gated_conv_activation=None" is NOT activation-free under a
depthwise gate, and kda-gated minus kda-plain varies the activation's position,
its learnability, AND the post gate together. Against this project's measured
within-arm SD of 0.01463 nats that yields a real effect nobody can attribute.

The arm that isolates the gate -- plain conv with NO activation -- was
unbuildable: _build_conv hard-coded activation=silu with no config knob. Adds
conv_activation (default "silu", so nothing existing moves) and a fourth cell:

    kda-plain        gated=False  conv_activation="silu"   as shipped
    kda-plain-noact  gated=False  conv_activation=None     THE BASELINE
    kda-gated        gated=True   gated_activation=None
    kda-gated-silu   gated=True   gated_activation="silu"

The gate contrast is kda-gated minus kda-plain-noact, and those two are
parameter-matched to exactly the 12,288/layer the gate costs.

FIVE MORE GUARDS THAT COULD NOT FIRE, OR FIRED ON THE WRONG THING:

- An unrecognised activation was accepted. fla's kernel matches 'silu'/'swish'
  EXACTLY and otherwise runs activation-free WITHOUT ERROR, so "Silu" raised on
  the reference path (what a CPU test exercises) and silently computed the
  None arm on GPU -- collapsing kda-gated-silu onto kda-gated while the config,
  the logs and the arm name all said silu. Now refused in __init__.
- The gated_conv=False guard did not check gate_structure -- the exact case its
  own comment was written about. gate_structure="lowrank" with gated_conv=False
  built three plain convolutions: two identically-trained controls under
  different arm names, i.e. a guaranteed null.
- No reset_parameters, so Transformer.init_weights' to_empty() + sweep left the
  gates as uninitialized memory for anything that skips a mixer's init_weights.
  short_conv.py documents shipping exactly this on the MQAR calibration.
- gate_source was accepted and then silently overwritten. Now derived from
  gate_structure, and a contradiction raises.
- The depthwise gate FLOPs term double-counted by 2x. Under 0.01% of the layer
  and the test bound is <1%, so it could not bite -- but arms are matched on
  this quantity.

MEMORY WAS UNDER-COUNTED BY 1.5x. Walking what autograd retains for
post*conv(pre*u): sigmoid saves its output, the scalar multiply's result is
retained as an operand, and pre*u is retained as the conv input -- 3 stream
tensors per gate in eager, not 2. So 576 MiB/layer and 15.75 GiB over 28 layers
against KDA's measured 5.169 GiB peak, about 4x rather than 3x. The default is
now the eager count, because an optimistic memory figure is the one that gets a
paid run OOM-killed. Also documents the two other 2x assumptions the estimate
hides: bf16 (mul type-promotes, so an fp32 param dtype doubles it) and no
activation checkpointing (which makes it ~free).

The lowrank RNG hazard is now recorded rather than half-stated: beyond the
disclosed gate_down draw, Transformer.init_weights runs its reset_parameters
sweep on the GLOBAL RNG at model.py:290, before the seeded generator exists at
:299 -- and lowrank adds nine nn.Linear submodules per layer. So a lowrank arm
is not seed-comparable to a plain arm. Depthwise is exempt (bare Parameters,
one Conv1d, matching what CausalConv1d is).

The GPU smoke now checks the two things no test covered: that the arms are
bit-identical at init THROUGH THE FUSED KERNEL (every CPU test compares the
reference path against a hand-written helper, i.e. a path the run never
executes), and that fla honours activation=None at all.

65 CPU tests, 7 fla-gated. 19 mutations, 0 survived, 0 no-op.

